{"severity":"error","file":"errors/protocol_invalid_1.march","start_line":28,"start_col":4,"end_line":28,"end_col":5,"message":"Protocol `Q`: this step can never run in the `choose` branch that ends in a `loop` — the steps after a `choose` are projected into EVERY branch. Move it into the `done` branch, after its last step. A branch with several steps lists them on the lines after `done ->`, one per line, indented under the label (no `do`/`end`).","code":"protocol_invalid","fix":null,"labels":[{"file":"errors/protocol_invalid_1.march","start_line":25,"start_col":22,"end_line":25,"end_col":23,"message":"this `loop` repeats forever"}],"notes":[],"category":"PROTOCOL"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/protocol_invalid_1.march","start_line":31,"start_col":2,"end_line":33,"end_col":5,"message":"`main` performs IO but declares no grant. The program reaches `IO.Console`; a `main` with no capability parameter is granted nothing.\nhelp: declare the grant `main` actually needs —\n        fn main(_cap_console : Cap(IO.Console)) : ()\nor grant everything with `fn main(cap : Cap(IO))`.\n`forge fix` can apply this.","code":"cap_grant","fix":{"kind":"replace","start_line":31,"start_col":9,"end_line":31,"end_col":11,"text":"(_cap_console : Cap(IO.Console))","applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
